{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>That he does not come near, etc., and there shall not be, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say <b>and there shall not be</b>, etc. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 110a) that this comes as a warning to one who maintains a dispute, that he transgresses the prohibition of ״וְלֹא יִהְיֶה״ etc. And aside from their approach of blessed memory, it appears that HaShem intended to give a reason why this reminder was necessary, and why the warning already in the Torah — ״לֹא יִקְרַב אִישׁ זָר״ (a stranger shall not come near), and whoever does come near, etc., the earth shall swallow him — did not suffice. For this He said <b>and there shall not be like Korah</b> — meaning: if I command without this reminder, I am concerned that the warning will not avail for some person among them, and he will die like Korah and his assembly; whereas this reminder will be effective, so that it will not come about for him to be as it was for Korah and his assembly." "<b>as HaShem spoke by the hand of Moses to him.</b> Meaning: because He said <b>and there shall not be like Korah</b> etc., from the implication of the matter you learn that anyone who rises up to contest the priesthood will have happen to him as happened to Korah and his assembly — yet this thing we do not find that HaShem had warned as such. Therefore He said <b>as HaShem spoke by the hand of Moses to him</b> — meaning, to Korah. From this you learn that the things Moses said to Korah — ״וְאִם בְּרִיאָה יִבְרָא ה׳ וּפָצְתָה הָאֲדָמָה אֶת פִּיהָ״ (and if HaShem creates a creation and the earth opens its mouth), etc. — were the words of HaShem by the hand of Moses to warn him, and Moses did not say them on his own. And that is what is meant by His saying <b>by the hand of Moses to him</b> — meaning, to Korah, who is mentioned just above."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:38.573999470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}